+// ArchiveManager is the package's high-level coordinator. It owns the
+// registry of supported formats and performs every common archiving task —
+// detecting the format of an archive or compressed file, creating archives
+// (optionally compressed), extracting archives to disk, gathering files from
+// disk, and presenting archive contents through the io/fs interfaces — by
+// selecting the right registered format and handing off to it.
+//
+// Coordination is the manager's only structural responsibility: the format
+// registry plus the thin one-call operations that dispatch to it. The tunable
+// behavior of each operation lives in its own cohesive option type —
+// FromDiskOptions (gathering), ArchiveOptions (ArchiveFolder), and
+// ExtractOptions (ExtractToFolder) — which the manager embeds as that
+// operation's defaults. To override a policy, set the field on the manager
+// (for example m.ExtractOptions.OverwriteExisting = true, or the equivalent
+// promoted m.OverwriteExisting); the flat field access is preserved for
+// compatibility. Prefix defaults the rooting of the file systems that
+// FileSystem returns.
+//
+// Because the manager owns its own format registry, embedding programs can
+// create isolated managers that support only a subset of the formats (or their
+// own custom formats) instead of relying on package-global state. All
+// package-level convenience functions (Identify, FileSystem, FilesFromDisk,
+// and RegisterFormat) delegate to DefaultArchiveManager, which is
+// pre-registered with every built-in format.
+type ArchiveManager struct {
+	// formats is the registry of formats this manager supports, keyed by
+	// the format extension without the leading dot.
+	formats map[string]Format
+
+	// FromDiskOptions are the on-disk gathering defaults applied by
+	// FilesFromDisk (and thus ArchiveFolder) when a caller does not supply
+	// its own FromDiskOptions. See FromDiskOptions for field semantics.
+	FromDiskOptions
+
+	// ArchiveOptions are the defaults applied by ArchiveFolder.
+	ArchiveOptions
+
+	// ExtractOptions are the defaults applied by ExtractToFolder.
+	ExtractOptions
 
-	// Prefix is the subdirectory that returned virtual file systems are
-	// rooted in by default; it mirrors ArchiveFS.Prefix. An empty Prefix
-	// roots file systems at the archive root, which preserves the
-	// historical behavior.
+	// Prefix is the subdirectory that FileSystem roots the virtual file
+	// systems it returns in by default; it mirrors ArchiveFS.Prefix. An
+	// empty Prefix roots file systems at the archive root, which preserves
+	// the historical behavior.
 	Prefix string
 }
 
